<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Defaults. This file is in git, so it holds placeholders and nothing else.

  Do not put your database password or your server's address in here. Run
  configure-server.bat in the root of the repository instead: it writes
  Config.local.xml, which is read in preference to this file and is ignored by
  git, so a real password cannot be committed by forgetting.

  Everything below works as it stands for a server on the machine you are
  sitting at, played by that machine only, once the database details are
  filled in.
-->
<Config>

  <!--
    THE TWO KINDS OF ADDRESS, which are easy to mix up and behave very
    differently when you do.

    ListenIP is what the engines BIND to. It decides who is able to reach
    them at all.

        127.0.0.1   only this machine. The default, and right for testing.
        0.0.0.0     every network card. Needed for anyone else to connect.

    ZoneIP and ChatIP are what the server TELLS THE CLIENT to connect to
    next. Logging in is a relay: the login engine hands the client off to a
    zone, and the zone hands it off to chat, each by address. So these must
    be an address the PLAYER can reach, which is not always the one the
    server binds to.

        127.0.0.1        players on this machine
        192.168.x.x      players on your network
        your public IP   players on the internet, with the ports forwarded
        a hostname       resolved at handoff, so a changing address is fine

    Getting this wrong has one obvious symptom: login works, character
    selection works, and then the client hangs or drops on entering the
    world. That is the handoff, sending the player to an address only the
    server itself can reach.
  -->
  <ListenIP>127.0.0.1</ListenIP>
  <ZoneIP>127.0.0.1</ZoneIP>
  <ChatIP>127.0.0.1</ChatIP>

  <!--
    The inter-server channel, which the engines use to talk to each other.
    It is unauthenticated: anything that can reach this port can act as one
    of the engines. Leave it on loopback unless you have firewalled it
    yourself, and never set it to 0.0.0.0 to "make things work".
  -->
  <CommListenIP>127.0.0.1</CommListenIP>

  <!-- Ports. The client is told these along with the addresses above. -->
  <LoginPort>7500</LoginPort>
  <ZonePort>7501</ZonePort>
  <ChatPort>7012</ChatPort>
  <CommPort>6996</CommPort>

  <!--
    The database. See Documentation/Running-a-server.md for creating it and
    loading the schema.

    These are placeholders and will not connect. Put the real ones in
    Config.local.xml, not here.
  -->
  <SQLType>MySql</SQLType>
  <MysqlConnection>Database=omnicell;Data Source=localhost;User ID=omnicell;Password=CHANGEME;SslMode=None</MysqlConnection>

  <!-- Logging -->
  <SqlLog>true</SqlLog>
  <LogChat>false</LogChat>

  <!-- Shown to players as they enter. {0} becomes the name and version. -->
  <Motd>Welcome to OmniCell {0}</Motd>

  <!-- en, de, ro. Default en. -->
  <Locale>en</Locale>

  <!--
    Diffie-Hellman parameters for the login handshake. Protocol constants
    shared with the game client, not secrets: changing them requires a
    patched client and will stop every unpatched one from logging in.
  -->
  <LoginDhPrivateKey>7ad852c6494f664e8df21446285ecd6f400cf20e1d872ee96136d7744887424b</LoginDhPrivateKey>
  <LoginDhPrime>eca2e8c85d863dcdc26a429a71a9815ad052f6139669dd659f98ae159d313d13c6bf2838e10a69b6478b64a24bd054ba8248e8fa778703b418408249440b2c1edd28853e240d8a7e49540b76d120d3b1ad2878b1b99490eb4a2a5e84caa8a91cecbdb1aa7c816e8be343246f80c637abc653b893fd91686cf8d32d6cfe5f2a6f</LoginDhPrime>
</Config>
